==Battleground==
*The enemy base here is a [[Doge Base (Enemy Base)|Doge Base]].
*Infinite [[Aku Doge]]s spawn after 10 seconds<sup>300f</sup>, delay 23.33~33.33 seconds<sup>700f~1,000f</sup>.
*1 [[Aku Doge]] spawns after 30 seconds<sup>900f</sup>.
*3 [[Aku Doge]]s spawn after 60 seconds<sup>1,800f</sup>, delay 1~2 seconds<sup>30f~60f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 99% HP:
**1 [[Aku Doge]] spawns as the boss.
**15 [[Aku Doge]]s spawn, delay 6.67~10 seconds<sup>200f~300f</sup>.
**5 [[Aku Gory|Aku Gories]] spawn, delay 20~23.33 seconds<sup>600f~700f</sup>.
**2 [[Oldhorn]]s spawn, delay 20 seconds<sup>600f</sup>.
**1 [[Midnite D.]] spawns.

==Strategy==
Try to stall against the beginning Aku Doges with Rock and [[Cat Cactus]] in order to build up money, as otherwise the stage can be rather tricky to pull off due to the very low amount of cash dropped by enemies before you hit the base. On average it takes around 2 Cacti per Aku Doge if your Cactus is around level 45, but you can use [[Future Cat]] as a filler meatshield against the starting waves of multiple Aku Doges, as Cactus on its own cannot stall them indefinitely. If you have it, [[Maize Cat (Rare Cat)|Cone]] works very well in this stage, though you will have to bring a Wave Shield unit as otherwise your stack will push much harder and can get shredded by the Doge Cannon.

Once you hit the base, lure the enemies out of the Doge Cannon's range (a bit over halfway through the stage) before sending out your large units. [[Elder Beast Naala (Special Cat)|Naala]] works very well here, as her Strong against Relics as well as wave immunity allow her to both be a great source of chip damage against the Oldhorns but also avoid any waves fired by the Doge Cannon. She is also a great damage dealer against both Aku Gory and Midnite D, as her LD allows her to stand out of reach from Aku Gory (and then switch to target Oldhorn) and at the same time still hit Midnite D. [[Master Uril (Special Cat)|Uril]] (even better in true form) can stall the Oldhorns, as while they are not the most important threats in this stage they still act as a wall for the other enemies as well as mow down anything within range. [[Cossack Cat (Rare Cat)|Royal Guard]] can greatly assist in chipping them down, as his Massive Damage against Relics allows him to mow through them at a quick pace, provided you keep your Royal Guard stack alive.

==Trivia==
*Like all [[Bazaar of the Pirate King]] stages, Stand By Motel is named after a movie, in this case ''[[:wikipedia:Stand By Me (film)|Stand By Me]]''.

